  "body": "Positioned within one of St Heliers’ most desirable coastal addresses in Auckland’s prestigious Eastern Bays, 20 Springcombe Road presents a rare opportunity to secure a substantial luxury coastal residence where architecture, lifestyle, and enduring quality come together with exceptional clarity. There are very few homes where everything feels so naturally resolved, where the morning light moves effortlessly through the living spaces, the coastal outlook becomes part of your daily rhythm, and coming home feels less like an arrival and more like an exhale.\r\n\r\nCompleted in 2021 following an extensive rebuild, the home was meticulously redesigned and reconstructed to create a beautifully resolved coastal estate of exceptional calibre. Privately positioned behind a timeless weatherboard façade, the residence unfolds across approximately 750 sq m of refined living, where expansive glazing, generous proportions and a prized north-facing orientation invite natural light deep into the interior while framing elevated coastal and sea views toward Rangitoto Island.\r\n\r\nThoughtfully conceived for both everyday living and sophisticated entertaining, the residence balances architectural sophistication with warmth, comfort, and effortless liveability. Beautifully connected indoor and outdoor spaces create an environment equally suited to quiet retreat, extended family living, long lunches with friends, and elegant entertaining on a grand scale.\r\n\r\nAt the centre of the home, an award-winning designer kitchen anchors the primary living domain, complemented by additional culinary and hosting spaces, including a well-appointed butler’s pantry and dedicated entertaining areas that allow the home to transition seamlessly\r\nfrom intimate gatherings to larger occasions with ease.\r\n\r\nAccommodation comprises five bedrooms and six bathrooms, including a privately positioned primary suite where elevated sea views, generous dressing, a refined ensuite, and covered outdoor living create a retreat-like environment of privacy and calm. A heated swimming pool, spa, gym and fitness studio, media room and beautifully appointed pool house complete a private leisure environment designed for relaxation, connection and everyday enjoyment.\r\n\r\nExtensive engineering consideration, integrated smart home technology, and enduring construction quality underpin the residence throughout, delivering comfort, capability, and confidence in equal measure, both now and for years to come.\r\n\r\nOccupying approximately 1,002 sq m of land (more or less), moments from St Heliers Beach, village cafés, coastal walkways, and approximately 10 kilometres from Auckland CBD, the property offers an exceptional balance of coastal lifestyle and urban accessibility.\r\n\r\nA compelling opportunity to secure one of Auckland’s most complete luxury coastal residences, where architectural integrity, liveability, and long-term quality are brought together in a home designed to be lived in fully and enjoyed for generations to come.\r\n\r\nContact Details \r\nKelly Brown  +64 21 471 661 | kelly.brown@nzsir.com\r\nJackie Parker  +64 21 505 520 | jackie.parker@nzsir.com\r\n\r\nDeadline Sale closing Thursday 25th June 2026 at 4:00 p.m. (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nImportant: This property may be marketed as suitable for overseas purchasers. However, this does not constitute confirmation of eligibility, approval, or suitability for any individual buyer. All overseas purchasers remain subject to New Zealand’s overseas investment laws, including the Overseas Investment Act 2005, and may require consent from the Overseas Investment Office. You must obtain your own independent legal, financial, and technical advice and secure any necessary approvals before proceeding with a purchase.",
